            "text": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The conversation history before this point was compacted into the following summary:\\n\\n<summary>\\n## Goal\\nGet the current weather in Tokyo using the `get_weather` tool and report it in one short sentence.\\n\\n## Constraints & Preferences\\n- Must use `get_weather`\\n- Answer in one short sentence\\n\\n## Progress\\n### Done\\n- [x] Called `get_weather(city=\\\"Tokyo\\\")`, which returned: \\\"Tokyo: clear25°C, wind 10 km/h\\\"\\n- [x] Answered: \\\"Tokyo is clear at 25°C, with 10 km/h wind.\\\"\\n\\n### In Progress\\n- [ ] (none)\\n\\n### Blocked\\n- (none)\\n\\n## Key Decisions\\n- **Used `get_weather` with city=\\\"Tokyo\\\"**: The user explicitly asked for this tool.\\n- **Replied in a single sentence**: This followed the user's brevity constraint.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n1. (none) The task is complete. Wait for a new user request.\\n\\n## Critical Context\\n- Tokyo weather result: clear, 25°C, wind 10 km/h\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\\n\\n## Original Request\\nThe user asked \\\"Is that warm? One word.\\\" This is the only message in the conversation so far. It asks for a one-word answer. \\\"That\\\" has no referent in the visible context, so it is unclear what the user is asking about (for example, an item, a temperature, or an image or attachment that is not shown).\\n\\n## Progress So Far\\n- The assistant has not replied yet.\\n- No work, decisions, or clarifications have happened.\\n- No attachments, files, or other details identifying \\\"that\\\" appear in the messages above.\\n\\n## Context Needed to Continue\\n- The user wants a one-word answer about whether something is \\\"warm.\\\"\\n- What \\\"that\\\" refers to is unspecified. Later messages may supply it. If they do not, the assistant may need to ask what the user means.\\n- The one-word format constraint should be respected in any reply.\\n</summary>\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"low\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Yes.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Should I bring an umbrella? One word.\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"low\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"No.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Thanks. One word.\",\"cache_control\":{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\":\"low\"}}],\"max_tokens\":128000,\"stream\":true,\"system\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"You are a weather assistant. Answer briefly.\\n\\n<addendum>\\nReference for pi-restore-openrouter-claude-sonnet-5-5-compaction: the weather desk's station catalog. Use it only when asked.\\n- Station 1: code WX001, elevation 0 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 2: code WX002, elevation 37 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 3: code WX003, elevation 74 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 4: code WX004, elevation 111 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 5: code WX005, elevation 148 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 6: code WX006, elevation 185 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 7: code WX007, elevation 222 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 8: code WX008, elevation 259 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 9: code WX009, elevation 296 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 10: code WX010, elevation 333 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 11: code WX011, elevation 370 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 12: code WX012, elevation 407 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 13: code WX013, elevation 444 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 14: code WX014, elevation 481 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 15: code WX015, elevation 518 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 16: code WX016, elevation 555 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 17: code WX017, elevation 592 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 18: code WX018, elevation 629 m, reports hourly.\\n- Station 